    "answer": {
      "short": "$49$ square units. Equal perimeters give $4x+8=6x-2$, so $x=5$.",
      "worked": "The ticks show that all four sides of the square have length $x+2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P_{\\text{square}}&=4(x+2)=4x+8\\\\P_{\\text{rectangle}}&=2(2x)+2(x-1)=6x-2\\end{align*}$$\n\nEquate the perimeters and subtract $4x$ from both sides:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4x+8&=6x-2\\\\8&=2x-2\\\\10&=2x\\\\5&=x\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe square has side length $5+2=7$.\n\n$$A=7^2=49$$\n\nIts area is $49$ square units. Check: both perimeters are $28$ units.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
